<http://data.silknow.org/object/a3cf8950-7315-3cec-950b-ed31779022ac/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress of red silk machine-made net, with high waist, low neck and short, slightly gathered sleeves. The bodice is cut with side panels used on the cross, and fastens at the centre back with a narrow red silk ribbon at the waistline. The skirt is cut straight with additional fullness gathered at the centre back. It is hand stitched. \n\nThe neckband and sleeves and a v-shaped insertion in the bodice front are embroidered with a design of rosebud garlands worked in pink, red and green chenille. This embroidery is repeated at the hem, with a wider trail of roses and rosebuds.\n\nBefore the dress was donated, it apparently had a red under-dress which was not brought to the Museum because it was 'very perished'."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a3cf8950-7315-3cec-950b-ed31779022ac> .

